			"notes": "Ornithe libraries (OSL and friends) ship .classtweaker files, the accesswidener successor. They carry the same intermediary token soup, so both the converter's text-resource rewrite and the plugin's residue scan now handle them like accesswideners.\n\nThose same libraries are multi-version and compiled against the newest version in their range, so they reference members that do not exist in b1.7.3. Calamus numbers every version separately, so there is nothing to convert those tokens to. The post-conversion residue check now splits leftovers into tokens the b1.7.3 map actually covers (real gaps, still a warning) and the rest (logged at info instead of shouting about a gap that cannot exist).\n\nAlso drops the b1.7.3 method entries that never existed there.\n\nMod and gradle plugin both at 1.0.4."
		},
